From 4ae434ddfdc0b727d853df4e67e451682954fd7a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arena Agent <agent@arena.ai>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 16:49:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Booking requests: today by default, filters that filter, and
 answering for a salon

The tab opened on "Today" and listed every request ever taken, because the date
range never reached the list endpoint. It does now, and the endpoint resolves
the window in IST (midnight to midnight) and echoes it back, so the chip line
and the table always name the same window.

- Changing any filter returns to page 1. Filtering from page 3 of a list that
  has one page asked for page 3 and showed nothing.
- Status is a chip row carrying the server's own counts for the selected
  window, so the number on a chip and the rows it produces are one number.
- The table is `table-layout: fixed` with an ellipsis on every text column and
  the full value in its title, so a long salon, customer or service name
  shortens instead of widening the page past the sidebar. The layout's main
  column also gets `min-width: 0`, which is the actual fix for content
  escaping the sidebar rail.
- An admin can accept or decline a request on a salon's behalf, with a note
  (required when declining). The request stays visible behind the confirmation
  and the buttons name the salon. Rows answered by My Naai say so, in the
  table, in the lifecycle and in the CSV.

The answer goes through the salon's own accept path on the server, so the
request can still only ever become one booking.
